          "type": "numerical",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "The periodic table consists of 18 groups. An isotope of copper, on bombardment with protons, undergoes a nuclear reaction yielding element $X$ as shown below. To which group, element $X$ belongs in the periodic table?\r\n\r\n${ }_{29}^{63} \\mathrm{Cu}+{ }_{1}^{1} \\mathrm{H} \\rightarrow 6_{0}^{1} n+{ }_{2}^{4} \\alpha+2{ }_{1}^{1} \\mathrm{H}+\\mathrm{X}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [],
          "correctValue": "8",
          "solution": {
            "text": "${ }_{29}^{63} \\mathrm{Cu}+{ }_{1}^{1} \\mathrm{H} \\rightarrow 6{ }_{0}^{1} n+{ }_{2}^{4} \\mathrm{He}+2{ }_{1}^{1} \\mathrm{H}+{ }_{Z}^{A} X$\r\n\r\nBalancing the atomic mass and atomic number\r\n\r\n$63+1=(6 \\times 1)+4+2+A \\Rightarrow A=52$\r\n\r\n$29+1=(6 \\times 0)+2+2+Z \\Rightarrow Z=26$\r\n\r\nThus ${ }_{Z}^{A} X={ }_{26}^{52} X$ or ${ }_{26}^{52} \\mathrm{Fe}$\r\n\r\nHence, $X$ belongs to group 8 in the periodic table.",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
